						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, November 06, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Shades of Truth </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Greetings fellow Norrathians. This is Kikekia Silverheart from the sweet server of Solusek Ro here just saying that the Shades of Truth has opened its gates and are accepting newbies ahem new members in the guild. If you are interested in joining the honoring ranks of the Shades of Truth, please send a tell to Kreylyn, Rozen, Jerms, or Siluette. Tell them Kikekia sent you. or Kik sent me. thats the key word becuase i will invite anyone who asks me so i need to give them my approval of you. So just tell them i sent you and youll get in. Also youll be doing a huge favor for me by adding tallies to my recruiters list and get me closer to be an officer. Thank you for your support. The real truth is out there...you just need a good guild to help you sift through the shadows. Join the Shades of Truth.
							<br><BR>
							 - Kikekia Silverheart<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=421">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, October 31, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">BattleGuild.com </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Greetings!<BR><BR>I come before you in the Bardic tradition, to announce a new website for Bards.  Come and visit http://eqbards.battleguild.com<BR><BR>Regards, <BR><BR>Ardenn Musicstorm<BR>The Great Musical Kitty<BR>Maestro of Necessary Evil<BR>Realm Admin BattleGuild.com
							<br><BR>
							 - Ardenn Musicstorm<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=419">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Wednesday, October 22, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Amazonia'a New Website </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hey all you Solusekers!  Amazonia found a new home for their website and things will be changing dramatically, soon.  Our talented webmistress Neite is working feverishly at it.  Our new address is <a href="http://amazonia.lyssara">http://amazonia.lyssara.com</a> and you can still read our forums at <a href="http://pub162.ezboard.com.btheeqgirls">http://pub162.ezboard.com.btheeqgirls</a> until we move those, to a better place, too.<BR><BR>Hope to see you there!
							<br><BR>
							 - Deena<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=418">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, October 09, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Syndicate Ro </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hail Norrath,<BR><BR>A dark rider bearing a blood-stained scroll has crossed dangerous territory and risked life to bring you word from the Syndicate Ro Castle. <BR><BR>The Empire is seeking honorable members who have a keen ability to roleplay their characters. <BR><BR>Syndicate Ro is not a guild for those who wish to enter a leveling or loot contest. We are the most organized guild in Norrath (visit www.syndicatero.com and you'll agree) and we focus on unity, honor, roleplaying, working on skills and other things. How fast you level is not a concern. How tweeked you are is not our primary focus. We have fun banquets and raids, but we do other unique things as well. <BR><BR>We have many members in the 40s and 50s, but allow membership from levels 20 and above.<BR><BR>You are invited to take a tour of our castle http://www.syndicatero.com to see if your skills will best serve this highly organized empire known as Syndicate Ro - The future of Norrath.<BR><BR>Signed,<BR>Prince Venefix
							<br><BR>
							 - syndicatero<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=417">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, September 11, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Might and Honor </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Might and Honor as been reactivated and is now openly recruiting. Please email Enchantraa@comcast.net for more info.
							<br><BR>
							 - Enchantraa<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=416">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, September 08, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Eternal Fellowships </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							"Hey there, Solusek Ro!"<BR><BR>"Gnome here.  I'm an officer of Eternal Fellowships, and I'm here to say hello on behalf of my guild to make our presence more widely known to the larger server community."<BR><BR>"Hello."<BR><BR>Gnome bows, and walks off stage.  A few seconds later, he comes running back onto stage, holding rear (which is smoking, atm), sweating profusely and shaking somewhat.  A red and a blue aura surround him shortly, then dissipate.<BR><BR>"Umm, Caulda says I have to talk some more."  Gnome then winces.  Six seconds pass and he winces again.<BR><BR>"We're a few months over a year old now.  Under Caulda's leadership we've... " Gnome winces. "...grown, raided, and leveled.  The whole time, through and thr..."  Gnome winces. "..OOoh, we've always had fun, and lots of it.  This..." Gnome winces again. "... is actually somewhat funny - I guess she landed a replenishment and a..." Gnome winces. "..swarming death on me simultaneously.  That was after the nuke..." A bit of Winter's Frost hits Gnome again.  He returns fire offstage.  The DoT finally overtakes his regen, and Gnome keels over.<BR><BR>Caulda comes from offstage, her hair somewhat frazzling with electrictiy.  "As Gnome was saying, we always have a lot of fun, especially late night."  Gnome respawns and loots his corpse.  "We raid a few times a week, and we're working heavily on getting members flagged for the higher end PoP zones.  We're looking forward to LDoN, and looking forward to seeing more of you folks."<BR><BR>Gnome snares Caulda, then finishes speaking.<BR><BR>"We've got a new website, administrated by Taiddor, and hosted by Sivacholomunga at www.eternalfellowships.com.  We're not actively recruiting in the spam-the-/shout-in-every-zone way, but we're always interested in quality people.  Come check out our website or see some of us in-game!  Thank you for your time!"<BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - Gnoimnotanome<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=415">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, August 29, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Hey All Guild Forum Admins </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Recently there has been a bunch of different people spamming our fourms with their umm stuff... Most of the Guild Forums do NOT allow this that I visit.  <BR><BR>My best advice if your board is public is to place a notice that this is unacceptable posting practices.  Of course the delete button works great as well :p
							<br><BR>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=414">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, August 22, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Protectors of Moonglow recruiting changes... </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							The Protectors of Moonglow, a german speaking guild, soon reach their selfapplied hardcap of 50 players. We have to limit the last few slots for certain classes.<BR><BR>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Die Protectors of Moonglow sind eine deutschsprachige Gilde.<BR>Da wir unser selbstgestecktes Hardcap von 50 Spielern in der Gilde bald erreicht haben, kommen wir nicht umhin uns bei der Vergabe der letzten "freien" Plätze auf einige wenige Klassen zu beschränken. <BR><BR>Wir bieten noch folgenden Plätze an: <BR>2 mal Cleric <BR>1 mal Enchanter oder Barde <BR>1 mal Wizard oder Ranger <BR><BR>Bewerbungen anderer Klassen können wir leider nicht mehr in Betracht ziehen. <BR>-------------------------------------<BR>www.protectorsofmoonglow.org
							<br><BR>
							 - Ghumb (Guildleader)<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=412">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><BR><img src=images/redline.gif height=2 width="100%"><BR><BR></TD></TR>
					

						<TR><TD><p class="pTitle">New URL </p></TD></TR>
							<TR><TD><p class=pText>
							Our new web addy is http://my.hamilton.net/~bgeg/ much thx if you could change it on this site.
							 <BR><BR>- Poleslinger Longfellow<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=413">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp; <a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=413">[View Comments]</a>

					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, August 07, 2003</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Ssra Emp goes down with NO bane weapons </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Wednesday evening Necessary Evil entered the dreaded Emperor's chamber in Ssra Temple.  Yes, we were aware of the fact that bane weapons were not working.  We killed the Blood of Ssra and then proceded to take out the EMP himself while having NO dammage from melee weapons.  Pure proc and magic kill on the EMP.  I believe this is a Server first if not a EQ first.  This was also NE's FIRST EMP kill and only our second attempt at the mob.
							<br><BR>
							 - Kudelini<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=409">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=409">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>

